>
  <section id="ownership" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Ownership</h2>
    <p>
      Each work package owns the directory in the task board at <code>specs/00-overview.md</code> §4.
      An agent edits files inside that directory, plus shared files the WP spec lists explicitly.
      A change that crosses packages starts in the spec: edit the contract, and note it under
      “Change log” at the bottom of that spec, before editing the second package.
    </p>
    <p>
      The only shared files the overview’s parallelisation map allows an integrating agent to change
      are the root <code>package.json</code> workspaces, <code>tsconfig.base.json</code>, and
      <code>bun.lock</code>. Adding a new package’s own <code>package.json</code> is allowed. Two
      agents in the same wave do not edit the same directory.
    </p>
    <p>
      Code, comments, docs, and commit messages are English. Do not commit unless asked.
      <code>.reference/</code> is the legacy Next.js and Prisma tree: git-ignored, read-only domain
      knowledge. Nothing in v6 imports it. Do not copy a legacy module in verbatim.
      <code>specs/04-core-cam.md</code> is the overview’s pointer for legacy bugs that must not be
      reproduced.
    </p>
    <DocCallout title="Specs, then code">
      <p>
        <code>specs/</code> wins on contracts. <code>specs/roadmap/README.md</code> wins on
        sequence. The current step is the first <code>in progress</code> row, else the first
        <code>pending</code> row. That step is RM-01, <code>01-action-catalogue.md</code>. Do not
        use <code>specs/20-integral-roadmap.md</code> or <code>specs/21-integration-master-plan.md</code>
        as the queue. Open <code>specs/roadmap/00-how-to-follow.md</code> for the full agent rules.
      </p>
    </DocCallout>
    <p>
      Historical waves in §4 describe how WP0–WP14 were allowed to run together. They are not the
      remaining queue. Wave 1 was WP1, WP8, and a WP5 skeleton with a stub sidecar. Wave 2 was WP2,
      WP3, and WP6/WP7 against mocked API data. Wave 3 was WP4, then WP9 and WP10. Remaining ordered
      work is RM-00–RM-11.
    </p>
  </section>

