  <section id="done" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Definition of done</h2>
    <p>
      Every WP, from <code>specs/00-overview.md</code> §5. Every RM step adds the four checks in
      <code>specs/roadmap/README.md</code>: the index row is updated, the step spec change log has
      an entry, the cited design spec is updated if the surface changed, and the cross-phase AI
      invariants in <code>specs/20-integral-roadmap.md</code> still hold when the step touches tools,
      VCS, or workflows. That last file is an invariant list, not the sequence.
    </p>
    <ol>
      <li><code>bun install</code> at the repo root succeeds.</li>
      <li><code>bunx tsc -p &lt;package&gt;/tsconfig.json</code> exits 0 (strict, <code>noUncheckedIndexedAccess</code>).</li>
      <li><code>bun test &lt;package dir&gt;</code> passes. New behaviour has tests. A bug fix has a regression test.</li>
      <li>The public surface is documented in the WP spec. Update the spec if the surface changed.</li>
      <li>No imports from <code>.reference/</code>, no <code>any</code> in exported signatures, no <code>process.env</code> reads outside the config module.</li>
      <li><code>specs/01-conventions.md</code> is followed: English, <code>.ts</code> import suffixes, millimetres and radians, Effect v4 service shape, SQLite only from <code>packages/db</code>.</li>
    </ol>
    <DocCode language="bash" title="Replace core with the directory you own">
{`bun install
bunx tsc -p packages/core/tsconfig.json
bun test packages/core`}
    </DocCode>
    <p>
      Effect tests use <code>bun:test</code> and <code>Effect.runPromise</code> with the layers
      passed in. Database tests use <code>:memory:</code>, as
      <code>packages/db/src/database.test.ts</code> does. Do not mark an RM row <code>done</code>
      in the README until those commands pass for the directories the step owns.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section id="leave-alone" class="doc-section">
    <h2>Leave these alone</h2>
    <table>
      <thead>
        <tr><th>Do not</th><th>Do this instead</th></tr>
      </thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr>
          <td>Edit <code>apps/sidecar</code> while your step owns <code>packages/ai</code> only.</td>
          <td>Stay inside the owner directories on the current RM row. Cross the boundary in the spec first.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Start RM-04, RM-08, or RM-11 because the product area is familiar.</td>
          <td>RM-01 is current. RM-04 waits on RM-03. RM-08 waits on RM-07. RM-11 waits on RM-01 and RM-03.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Copy the roadmap’s 121/195 into <code>specs/00-overview.md</code>, or the reverse, without running coverage.</td>
          <td>Run <code>bun run --filter @cadcamfun/api coverage</code> and update the spec you were asked to update.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Add <code>packages/core/src/cam/program</code> because WP14’s Owns cell names it.</td>
          <td>That path is not in the tree. RM-02 is <code>pending</code> and is not the current step.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Import <code>.reference/</code> to finish a screen faster.</td>
          <td>Re-implement in SolidJS under the feature folder. The legacy UI is domain knowledge.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Commit the spec status flip yourself unless asked.</td>
          <td>Conventions: do not commit unless asked. The definition of done still requires the spec text to be updated in the working tree when the surface changed.</td>
        </tr>
        <tr>
          <td>Read <code>.env*</code> to learn which WP is “really” done.</td>
          <td>Status lives in <code>specs/00-overview.md</code> and <code>specs/roadmap/README.md</code>. Those env files are unused.</td>
        </tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </section>
